  "title": "Delhi Brings 'Cockroach' Protests to the Front Amid Security and Political Concerns",
  "summary": "Thousands of security personnel have been deployed in Delhi ahead of a major protest by the Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. The event is set to take place on October 10, with security measures including the closure of metro stations, cancellations of trains, and restrictions on internet access, as protesters seek to gather in Jantar Mantar.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Thousands of security personnel have been deployed in Delhi to prevent unauthorized gatherings in anticipation of the CJP protest.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A protest led by the CJP is set to take place on October 10, with security measures including the closure of metro stations and train services.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The protests have drawn attention to political tensions in the Indian government, with demands for judicial oversight and accountability being emphasized.",
      "confidence": 0.95
